#!/bin/sh
# scripts/hooks/l7r-hook <event> | setup - the one command each hook entry of .claude/settings.json calls (feature 451 T169).
#
# WHY A LAUNCHER (the GM 2026-11-23, specs/451-time-retro-and-efficiency/request.md "on hook output length"): the harness prints an
# entry's command with every block or notice it emits, and the entries' 239-330 character commands were 1.66M characters of one
# session's transcript, 6,665 stored occurrences (measured 2026-11-23). So each entry is `"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"/scripts/hooks/l7r-hook <event>`,
# held to 64 characters by tests/hooks/test-l7r-guard.sh, and what the commands carried is here:
#
# - THE MIRROR'S COPY FIRST: /diagram is main's mirror, so its scripts are what every session runs once they land (feature 449
#   research R6); the copy beside this file only where the mirror has none. This file is the project tree's own, found by
#   $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, which the harness sets for every hook. CLONE_MAIN is the mirror's test seam, as in scripts/sync-with-main.sh.
# - <event>: the Rust guards' one dispatcher, scripts/hooks/l7r-guard.sh (feature 449 T005). Each entry's timeout (60 s; PreToolUse
#   600 s) stays above the wrapper's 45 s build limit (L7R_GUARD_BUILD_SECS), so the wrapper's bounded build ends before the harness
#   kills the hook; the suite checks it.
# - setup: scripts/container/setup-dev-env.sh --ensure, SessionStart's other entry - a NEW hook, not a relaxed guard (2026-10-04, the
#   GM: a fresh container's setup built into our procedures as a quick no-op): it provisions a fresh container once and costs 30 ms
#   after; its 900 s timeout is a first install's.
#
# The commands also carried the guard-file guard's escape marker and its reason: the marker is that guard's escape for an edit of the
# settings, so it rode in the edited text. Its supported form is `make guard-edit FILE=.claude/settings.json WHY="<reason>"` (the
# reason in the guard log and the commit message), never a command every hook message repeats. This file is a guard file too, on
# both routes (rust/guard/src/guards/guard_file_hooks.rs, make_only_hooks.rs), its name distinct enough for make-only's name screen.
#
# POSIX sh, not bash: it runs before every guard call, and as dash it adds about 0.4 ms a call where bash added about 3 ms (100 calls
# into a stub, best of 3, 2026-11-23).
#
# THE DISPATCHER BY `bash`, NOT ITS SHEBANG (451 T456): `#!/usr/bin/env bash` started /usr/bin/env, uutils' multicall binary, about
# 3 ms before bash on every hook call - the chain 12.28 against 9.23 ms median, 40 runs, load 15.5, 2026-11-27
# (dev/measurements/2026-11-27/hook-floor/t456-launcher.txt). `bash` by PATH, as the setup line runs its script: dash's PATH search is
# a few stats and no fork, and no fixed path is assumed (here /bin/bash and /usr/bin/bash are one file, but a container need not be).
# The mirror-or-tree choice still asks the exec bit, so a copy not executable is passed over as before.
d=${0%/*} m=${CLONE_MAIN:-/diagram}
if [ "${1:-}" = setup ]; then
  s=$m/scripts/container/setup-dev-env.sh; [ -f "$s" ] || s=$d/../container/setup-dev-env.sh
  exec bash "$s" --ensure
fi
h=$m/scripts/hooks/l7r-guard.sh; [ -x "$h" ] || h=$d/l7r-guard.sh
# Idle: the Stop's background idle check (451 T183), an asyncRewake entry - its exit 2 wakes an idle session
[ "${1:-}" = Idle ] && exec bash "$h" --idle-check
exec bash "$h" "$@"
